Set the installed root before running commands:

```sh
AC_AGENTS_ROOT={{ assistant_install_root | quote }}
```

# Assistant team: commands

Run as the runtime user. One environment per user; credentials stay local.

`PROJECT` always means the project name. Each project has one team; its roles are
participants in that team, not separate projects. `ROLE` selects a participant
(such as `orchestrator` or `builder`); `ARCHIVE` selects a retained archive directory.

Ansible roles reproduce installation; source role READMEs describe validation limits.

```sh
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" --help             # every command, parameters and brief explanation
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" version            # installed source version/build
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" setup --list       # enabled / installed / credentials saved (not model verification)
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" setup             # choose profiles, then optional native login
cd "$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/model-environments/PROFILE"; ./login     # PROFILE: claude-work/priv, gemini-work/priv,
                         # codex-work/priv, mistral-work/priv (each full name)
./login --clear           # only current profile; exit CLI and stop using projects first
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" --list            # project names + status; alias: list-projects
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" create-project example
vi {{ assistant_install_root }}/projects/example/project.example.config                      # role -> enabled profile
vi {{ assistant_install_root }}/projects/example/assistant-prompt.md          # fill [Project] and [Role: Name]; # lines are comments
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" start example
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" attach example orchestrator                 # give task; Ctrl-B D detaches
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" watch example                               # live messages; Ctrl-C viewer only
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" status example
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" stop example
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" restart example
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" diagnostics --export /private/metadata.tar.gz # safe environment metadata
"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" apply-prompts example                       # effective next launch
```

Finish a project with one of these alternatives:
`"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" archive PROJECT` stops it if running and moves its full contents/config to
`{{ assistant_install_root }}/project-archive/PROJECT-ddmmyyhhmm` (local 24-hour time); `"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" destroy PROJECT` stops it if running and deletes it.
Both remove only its containers; account profiles and other projects stay intact.
Archive refuses same-minute or exact-name collisions before stopping. Rename the
project if an exact-name archive already exists. Named instances are disabled,
reset and forgotten; shared templates remain. Do not run same-project start/edit
operations concurrently.

List status describes services: running, starting, stopping, stopped, failed,
partial (orphan components) or unknown (metadata unavailable); it does not verify model access.

Artifacts: `{{ assistant_install_root }}/projects/example/workspace` (`/workspace/shared` in containers).
Vertex work profiles require the scoped Cloud SDK (operator-selected during deployment); private Gemini uses scoped Antigravity (`cd "$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/model-environments/gemini-priv"; ./login`, then `./agy`). Its team adapter is pending; use Gemini work for project roles.
Native SSH/container auth uses local file permissions, not encryption at rest.
Mistral native login is supported; team adapter is not implemented yet.
Login reports failed/cancelled or credentials saved/model access unverified; no automatic inference.
All eight role sessions start only after enabled assignments and saved auth pass; connectors lack service tools, observer snapshots are manual. Details: `{{ assistant_install_root }}/README.md`.

Human-readable diagnostics: `tail -f {{ assistant_install_root }}/environment-logs/events.log` (safe metadata only).

The editable default template for new projects is `{{ assistant_install_root }}/conf/templates/assistant.prompt.md.template`.
Creation copies its role instructions into the new project; existing project prompts
remain independent. Deployment preserves operator edits and migrates the old home-level
template without overwriting an existing destination. Conflicting paths require operator review.

`"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" unarchive PROJECT-ddmmyyhhmm` copies a retained archive to that dated project name, enables its target, and leaves it stopped. The original archive is always retained.

`"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" rename-project OLD NEW` stops and renames a project/config, preserving content and target enablement. It leaves NEW stopped: `"$AC_AGENTS_ROOT/bin/team" start NEW`. Never run same-project lifecycle commands concurrently.
